                    "url": "https://github.com/ktaranov/sqlserver-kit/blob/master/SQL%20Server%20Trace%20Flag.md",
                    "title": "sqlserver-kit/SQL Server Trace Flag.md at master",
                    "content": "* Enabling SQL Server Trace Flag for a Poor Performing Query Using QUERYTRACEON If a `USE HINT` conflicts with another query hint, or a trace flag enabled at the query level (such as by [QUERYTRACEON]), SQL Server will generate an error when trying to execute the query.** * Trace Flag 272 (for SQL Server 2012) * Trace Flag 1118 (for versions < SQL Server 2016) * Trace Flag 3023 (for versions < SQL Server 2014) * Trace Flag 3427 (for SQL Server 2016) * Trace Flag 6534 (for versions SQL Server 2012, 2014, 2016) (if use spatial data types) * Trace Flag 7745 (for versions >= SQL Server 2016 and Query Store enabled) * Trace Flag 7752 (for versions >= SQL Server 2016 and < 2019 and Query Store enabled) In SQL Server 2016 you can enable trace flag 3427 to bypass this overhead starting with SP1 CU2. **Trace flag 6534** enables performance improvement of query operations with spatial data types in SQL Server 2012, SQL Server 2014 and SQL Server 2016.",
