                {
                    "url": "https://medium.com/@adnanmasood/a-pragmatic-cdos-field-guide-to-data-quality-part-2-where-it-breaks-a-field-taxonomy-of-551ff3b7d5a8",
                    "title": "A Pragmatic CDO's Field Guide to Data Quality — Part 2 — ...",
                    "content": "We unpack a five-family taxonomy — business semantics & policy, identity/linkage (MDM), schema & pipeline, analytics & ML, governance & process — anchored in real-world outages. You’ll learn the signature failure modes (schema evolution gone wrong, CDC retractions, grain mismatches, missing consent flags), how to tag them for faster triage, and how to trace root cause with lineage so your post-mortems stop sounding like guesswork. * **Five Failure Families:** We catalog data quality failures into five families — (A) **Business Semantics & Policy**, (B) **Identity & Linkage (MDM)**, © **Technical Schema & Pipeline**, (D) **Analytics & ML**, (E) **Governance & Process** — with codes A1–A4, B1–B4, C1–C11, D1–D5, E1–E7. * **Symptom → Tag → Trace:** For each sub-code, we show how issues **surface** (symptoms like conflicting KPIs or duplicate records), how to **tag** incidents with the right code, and how to **trace** root cause via **data lineage**. Dr. Adnan Masood is an Engineer, Thought Leader, Author, AI/ML PhD, Stanford Scholar, Harvard Alum, Microsoft Regional Director, and STEM Robotics Coach.",
